00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.310
I'm sorry.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:23.250
At this point even if you come back,
there's no place for you on stage.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.050
Your contract's been terminated too.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.110
That was the obvious choice for me to make.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.150
Yes, I know.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.890
If you let me come back, I'll do anything.
I won't ask to be paid, either.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:38.130
I really do love Kaleido Stage. Please, Boss.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:41.200
If you're that set on being an unpaid gofer,
I've got no reason to stop you.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.750
Do what you want.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.930
Thank you, Boss!

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:50.810
It's the same as the first time I came to
Kaleido Stage by myself, to do the audition.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.210
A fresh start from zero.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.110
That time, my dream was to become
a Kaleido Star,

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:03.080
but this time it's a show everyone
can enjoy, with no battles.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:08.360
It might take time, but the path to being a
real star will open up for me too, I know it.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.690
Tea or coffee?

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.520
She's asking you if you'd like some tea.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.400
Forget the tea. How about a stylish cocktail or...

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:16.900
What?

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:17.200
Um...

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:17.200
What?

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:17.800
Um...

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:18.800
Oh, no thank you, I'm fine!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.240
What are you doing?!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.240
Oh, no thank you, I'm fine!

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:20.700
Oh, no thank you, I'm fine!

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.840
You're on a trip by yourself,
even though you're so young?

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.980
Hmm? Oh, yes. But I've got a lot of
friends in the United States.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.380
Oh, really? That's nice. Friends are
so important, aren't they?

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:37.150
Yes! They're all my really
really really good friends!

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.210
That's right... I'm not starting from zero.
I've got everyone with me now.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:49.760
"My Amazing Fresh Start"

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.830
My Amazing Fresh Start

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.830
"My Amazing Fresh Start"

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.700
My Amazing Fresh Start

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.680
Sora! Over here, over here!

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.680
Mr. Policeman!

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.510
Sora! Good to have you back!

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:06.980
Mr. Policeman, I can't breathe.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.680
I just don't understand
young people these days...

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.450
Whoops, sorry about that. I was just so happy.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.990
Thanks for coming to pick me up,
Mr. Policeman!

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.490
Everyone's waiting for you
to get back home, Sora!

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:19.360
I can't wait to see everyone!

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:23.500
Mr. Policeman,

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:29.370
because of what happened I figured out that
I really, really love Kaleido Stage.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:34.140
You should say that stuff in front of
everyone who's waiting for you.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.300
Yeah, you're right.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:43.120
Want some candy?

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.520
Sure, thanks.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.790
You know, I want to create a Kaleido Stage

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:49.690
where the audience and the cast
can all have fun.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.330
I like it when people smile.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.600
That's my Sora!

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.610
Welcome back, Sora!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.210
I... I'm home...

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.300
Sora!

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.350
Geez, Sora, I was really worried, you know!

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.020
I'm sorry, Rosetta.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.890
I didn't know what I'd do if
you hadn't come back.

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.690
Thank you for coming all the way to
Japan for me, Ken.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:23.860
What?!

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.660
Ken! You went to Japan?

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:28.500
It wasn't just me. I was with Mr. Policeman.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.200
No fair! Where's our Japan souvenirs?

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.630
Oh, that's right. Souvenirs, souvenirs...

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.400
For Miss Sarah, a Ninja Transformation Kit.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.740
For Mia, a good-luck charm.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:41.440
Oh, it's cute!

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.650
For Marion and Jonathan, hagoita paddles.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.200
Cool!

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.080
For Ken, a globe.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.240
Huh? A globe?

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.640
For Anna, a jester's mask and a slap fan.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.160
Sora, this thing has kind of a scary face.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.960
That's a Japanese lion.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.790
A lion?

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.300
Hey, Marion, she says this is a lion!

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.360
Wow!

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.600
Sora, are you really okay now?
You're recovered and everything?

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:08.240
I'm sorry, I guess I made everyone worry.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.170
But I'm okay now.

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:12.500
I won't lose sight of my dream anymore.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.510
I'm glad you're feeling better.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:18.150
I wonder why I got a globe...

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:20.080
Something that's only useful two or three
times in a person's whole life...

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.120
Something you don't miss if it's gone...

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.190
To you, I give this!

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:27.420
You'll be the fool and I'll be
the straight man! This'll be great!

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:31.160
How many times have I told you
I'm not going to pair up with you?!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.850
What? Why not?

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.760
Bloodlust! I sense bloodlust from someone!

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:37.030
You villain!

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:37.900
Huh?

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:38.990
May!

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.090
May?

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.110
I can't hear a word she's saying.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:46.010
She's barking.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.870
Wow, this glass is really soundproof.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:50.100
Hey, she's coming this way.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.340
Galaxy Warp Seven!

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:55.410
Congratulations on winning the
Circus Festival, May.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:58.040
What are you doing here?!

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:00.620
May, stop it.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.630
Even if her contract's been terminated,
Sora's one of us.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.230
Can't you even say "welcome back"?

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.030
"Welcome back"?! Oh please.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.800
You can't go onstage, and there's not
even a room for you in the dorm.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.470
Huh? No room?

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:16.870
Uh, we were going to explain that
after the party...

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:17.240
Oh... I guess that makes sense...

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.370
It's okay. You'll be a guest
in my room, okay Sora?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.370
Oh... I guess that makes sense...

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.480
It's okay. You'll be a guest
in my room, okay Sora?

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:23.710
It means this is no time for
you to be here partying.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.010
Hurry up and go see the Boss already!

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.320
Hurry up and get him to let you
back on the stage!

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.990
Because in my book, the festival isn't over yet.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:35.560
May...

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.490
So basically she wants Sora
to be back onstage?

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:40.500
Then why didn't she just come
right out and say so?

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.330
I just want to beat you fair and square, that's all!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:44.730
Thank you, May.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.500
But I'm fine with the way things are.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:47.470
Huh?!

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:48.530
Sora?

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:50.710
What do you mean by that?

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:54.330
I've decided not to fight battles anymore,
no matter what.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.380
You're saying... you don't intend
to go back onstage?

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.720
No, I haven't given up on the stage.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:03.420
I definitely want to go back onstage someday.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.390
But I don't want to do battle onstage.

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:09.520
I want to work with everyone
to create a fun show.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.360
That's my dream right now.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:12.590
Are you stupid?!

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:22.800
What do you think?

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.570
Yeah! It looks good on you!

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.840
Okay, Sora.

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:28.380
I'll be working for you all from now on.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:30.780
Whenever you want anything done,
please just give me a yell!

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:31.680
Welcome onboard!

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.040
Good luck!

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.120
One minute to curtain!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.150
Okay everybody, stay on top
of things today too!

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:42.620
Make especially sure you give it all you've got
during the Demon Spiral

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:46.190
and the scenes after that with
the two of us in them. Got it?

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.330
Got it!

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:47.600
None of you are fired up enough!

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.130
I really want Sora to go back onstage, though.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.130
None of you are fired up enough!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.400
I really want Sora to go back onstage, though.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.400
GOT IT!

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:55.200
Sora decided this for herself,
so let's support her.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:57.410
Someone get this set piece!

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.530
Got it, got it, got it!

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:00.840
Sora!

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.010
That might've been a little too heavy for me.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.480
Someone deliver these costumes quick!

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:06.850
Got it, got it, got it!

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.450
Sorry to make you do this, Sora.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.820
No problem.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:13.090
Take this one to passage 3B
and this one to passage 2C.

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:15.080
Okay, I got it!

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:28.560
It's Mr. Leon and May as Romeo and Juliet.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:52.420
Right now, Kaleido Stage belongs
to May and Mr. Leon.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.530
I'll leave the costumes here, okay?

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:56.690
Thanks, Sora.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:07.830
I thought I prepared myself for that. But...

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:15.510
But in the end...

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:19.810
I'm jealous of May and the applause
she's being showered with.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:27.960
I feel kinda bad for having you do this.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.200
No, I'm having fun.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:33.470
I'm getting to see lots of parts of
Kaleido Stage I didn't know about.

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:37.000
I want to know lots more about Kaleido Stage.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:40.070
You really love Kaleido Stage, don't you Sora?

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:41.840
Of course!

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:44.310
I'm gonna fall in love with it more and more!

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.550
Leon, so this is where you were.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.850
I told the people who messed up
the lighting today to be more careful.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.550
Leon?

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:00.090
Sora.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:09.430
Leon was watching Sora. Why?

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:24.720
Whoa, it's green.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:26.350
It's Japanese tea.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:27.820
Hmmm...

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:31.590
Well, well, well, I don't know if
you'll like it, but I hope so!

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:34.060
I'll drink it. I'll give it a try.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.490
Please do.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:42.160
It's bitter!

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.430
Once you get used to this stuff, it's pretty good!

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.810
Sora...

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:55.580
To be honest, I don't really get why
you don't want to battle onstage.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:12:02.060
I'm still proud of the time when I was aiming
to win consecutive world championships.

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:04.690
But according to you, is that a bad thing?

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:08.100
No, no, that's not what I think at all.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:09.200
But...

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.470
Of course you're amazing,

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:14.540
and I think May was great when she
won the festival too.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:18.140
I just figured out that those
weren't my dreams, that's all.

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:22.610
Is it okay if I dream of
being onstage with you, Sora?

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:26.050
Of course! I'm definitely going
to go back to the stage.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:29.180
And a show with you? I'd like
to do that right now!

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.390
Sora...

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.420
Oh, if you want more tea I can...

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.980
Oh, no more.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:43.600
La dadi dadi dadi dadi dadi dum.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.130
The oats have made a good harvest.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:47.570
La dadi dadi dadi.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.270
The green peas have made a good harvest too.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:54.540
Are there any bad children around?
Are there any sleepyheads around?

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.070
Good morning, Sora!

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:00.910
Fool, what are you doing?

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:06.120
You're the one who asked me to wake you up
quietly so Rosetta wouldn't wake up too.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.820
That's right! I have cleaning duty
first thing in the morning!

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.920
Well then, I'll just cuddle up with Rosetta and...

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:12.290
Ah!

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:15.230
Sora, I have something important to tell you!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:16.800
It's Layla! Layla's coming!

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.570
I can't believe you, telling lies about
Miss Layla. That's so low!

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:20.770
No, I'm telling you, it's true!

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:23.770
I didn't manage to tell you before,
but according to my fortunetelling

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:26.540
Layla's constellation, Leo, is very close by!

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:34.150
Well, I'll tell you flat-out, yesterday was boring.

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:37.180
It didn't make me feel a thing.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:42.990
The individual stunts may be attention-grabbers,
but the thing as a whole isn't a coherent show.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:46.120
Right, it's like a bunch of one-man
shows jumbled together.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.790
Mia, let's hear your opinion as the director.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:55.430
Mia, this is Cathy Timor.
She's a noted off-Broadway director.

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:58.910
Well, I'm just a layman outside
my area of expertise,

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.810
but I just gave you my honest feelings about it.

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:05.810
I... I'm sorry. I think Miss Cathy
is absolutely right.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:09.220
But I wasn't able to do anything...

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:14.060
It's my fault. It's all my fault. I'm very sorry!

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:17.260
Am I fired? I am fired, aren't l?

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:21.750
That's why Miss Cathy is here. I understand.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.100
You're interesting.

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:25.700
You've got talent.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.470
That I'll admit.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.600
That... "Demon Spiral," wasn't that
what it was called?

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:34.210
Making that work within Romeo and Juliet,
that's not a bad concept.

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:36.480
The character adaptations are chic too.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.780
As a setup, I think it's quite good.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.580
The problem is your directing ability.

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:45.320
Right now our attendance rate isn't dropping,

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.560
but the demographics of the audience
are drastically unbalanced.

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:49.720
I'd like your help correcting that trend.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.030
I'll take on this job.

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.100
Okay! Now that that's settled, let's go, Mia!

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.060
Huh?

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:59.500
Don't "huh?" me. I'm an outsider here,
so it won't work if you're not there, will it?

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.130
Uh, right!

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:14.320
Ugh, that's no good at all!

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:17.120
Leon and May, your timing wasn't
in synch at all right there!

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:18.450
Why were you so off?

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:21.990
Oh, that's because in performance
May can't get very much height,

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:25.090
so when Mr. Leon compensates,
his maneuver ends up looking small,

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:25.560
so that's why it looks...

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:26.260
The audience doesn't care about stuff like that!

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:26.260
so that's why it looks...

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:28.060
The audience doesn't care about stuff like that!

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.660
Leon, May, come here a minute!

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:35.340
Leon, I get that your skill is amazing
and everything, okay?

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:38.600
So show me something that
makes my heart pound more.

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:42.540
May, your performance in New York
made my blood thrum in my veins,

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.570
but what was WITH you just now?

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:47.650
Come on, a Romeo who's satisfied
as long as he's shining

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:50.120
and a Juliet who's terrified of being hated?

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.790
That's not going to get anyone excited!

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:54.890
Don't take your audience lightly!

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:56.090
Okay, take five!

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.180
She's cool...

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:02.000
Did you find her?

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.400
No, she's not anywhere.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:06.000
I'm sure she said she had
cleaning duty this morning...

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.430
Miss Layla's here and everything!

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.300
There she is!

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:15.780
Hi everybody!

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.380
What are you doing?

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:19.550
Just what it looks like. I'm wiping the windows.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:22.650
This part was a little smudged,
and it just started bugging me.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.850
Never mind about that, Miss Layla is here!

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:28.520
Sora!

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.790
Wow, that surprised me.

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.130
Sora, hurry!

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.930
Someone from Broadway named
Cathy is with her too.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:41.600
Miss Cathy too?

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:45.540
Oh... but at the festival...

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:48.180
I'm disappointed in you, Sora.

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:52.440
That's what she said to me, so
I don't know how to face Miss Layla.

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.240
Hey!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.450
You're hesitating and stopping short
over every little thing!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.680
And you call yourself Sora?!

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.790
The Sora I know tries it rather
than thinking about it.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:06.030
Or do you mean to never see Miss Layla
again for your whole life?

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:07.090
Rosetta...

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.300
Let's go!

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:10.900
You might have a chance too, Sora!

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.020
Huh?

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.500
A chance to go back to the stage... But...

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:18.940
All right, play it back for us.

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:20.840
Yes, Miss.

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.480
See, even you can tell, can't you?

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:26.080
What's with this listless performance?

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.950
Like right here, for instance.

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:29.940
Can you show us that bit one more time?

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.450
Rewind about thirty seconds.

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:33.510
All right.

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:37.720
The two of you aren't trying to
look at each other at all.

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:41.590
There's never been a pair of lovers like this.

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:43.030
Rosetta, wait.

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:44.570
Oh, just come on!

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.590
I can just sneak a look and...

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.600
Oh, hello.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.940
Sora, what are you doing?!

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:55.070
Oh, look, it IS Sora!

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:00.610
Hey, would you come down here for a sec?

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:03.080
I want to see you do Juliet!

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:07.150
I know you're not contracted anymore,
but just give it a try!

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.020
Leon...

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:16.760
Well, Sora? You've gotten your
chance right away.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:23.040
Sora, even if you want to avoid the battle,

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.470
it looks like the people around you
aren't going to let that happen.

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:27.870
Kalos won't complain. There's no problem!

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.640
Come on, what's the matter?

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.480
Come on, let's see it!

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:34.710
Let's see your Juliet!

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:40.790
I won't do it.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:41.890
What?

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:44.150
Please continue with May as Juliet.

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:54.440
Don't make me laugh!

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.100
What do you mean, you don't want to battle?!

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:58.330
You're just running away from
the competition, that's all!

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.040
You coward!

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.610
May...

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:10.620
Sora.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.350
Yes?

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.350
Sora.

00:19:11.590 --> 00:19:16.990
You should think carefully about how much
your attitude just now hurt May.

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:20.590
There are times when you can hurt
someone by not fighting too.

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:27.800
Good work today!

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:29.070
Yeah, you too!

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:31.940
Don't let what happened today
get to you too much, okay?

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:33.410
Yeah.

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:36.080
You cheer everyone up
just by being around, Sora.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.450
Even if you're not onstage.

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:41.480
I think you can just do what you think is right.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:42.850
Ken...

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:44.880
Thank you, Ken!

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:47.890
Hey, Ken, are you coming or what?

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:49.120
I'm coming!

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.260
Okay, see you tomorrow.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.990
Right. Good work today!

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:01.770
Thank you, Ken.

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:07.630
Mr. Leon...

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:12.080
Leon?

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:22.120
Didn't you want to become my partner?

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.990
My dream is different now.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:28.460
I think my goals are different from yours.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:33.930
The idea of a stage without any battling
might be just a fantasy,

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:38.700
